% A query whose plan computes is gathered, since any binding may fail it
% and no row may be delivered before nothing can; one that assigns from a
% term alone streams, since the variable it assigns is a function of those
% bound before it.  A wildcard still gathers, since two bindings differing
% only under it would give one row twice.
v(1). v(2).
w(a, b). w(a, c).

v(X), Y = X?
v(X), Y = X * 2?
w(X, _), Y = X?
